  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be completed before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (HO/CU/0506/001, received 7 June 2021; Proposed Shop Front Layout received 21 July 2021; Waste Management Plan, Waste Storage Area Plan, Waste Storage Elevations received 23 July 2021; HO/CU/06-06/002.01 received 26 July 2021) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - Delivery and collection times (including refuse) for commercial premises, which are situated in or very near to residential areas shall only be carried out between the following hours: Monday to Saturday between 07:00 and 22:00, Sunday between 09:00 to 20:00.",
    "Condition : 4 - The use hereby permitted for A3 purposes shall not be open to customers outside the following times: Monday to Friday 06:00 - 23:00, Saturday 08:00 - 23:00 and Sunday 8:00 - 23:00.",
    "Condition : 5 - The approved refuse and recycling area as shown on approved plan named Revised Waste Storage Area shall be completed and made available for use before the development hereby permitted is first occupied or brought into use, and thereafter shall be retained for such use at all times without obstruction. Bins shall be stored within the store at all times and shall not be left on the public highway. Non-recyclable and perishable waste shall be removed from site no less frequently than once a week. Waste shall be removed from the site to a suitable enclosed private storage area or an authorised refuse disposal or recycling site as soon as the bins become full if this is earlier than the time of the normal collection unless additional covered and enclosed bins (have been provided and are thereafter made permanently available for the on-site storage of refuse and waste."
  ],
